A||||5||GT Bastard||To anyone who pulled/installed their V6 through the top...||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-06-2001||07:46 PM||||Next week I'm pulling the block from my Fiero.  The top end is already removed, and the new bottom end is at the machine shop.  Bellhousing and mounts are disconnected, but does anyone know if you can pull the block without having to remove the waterpump/timing cover and pullies?  It looks like it'll work...  I wanted to keep the front of the motor intact so that it's easier to setup the wiring harness and brackets on the new motor.  Any tips out there?  I've helped install a couple 2.8's in Fiero's, but I wasn't involved the whole time, so I'm unsure about little stuff.  Next thursday is the BIG DAY for the Fiero hopefully.  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">     <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shaun41178||07-06-2001||11:14 PM||||you shouldn't have to remove that stuff except for the a/c maybe but the waterpump pulley will probably need to come off.  Other then that make some eye hooks and hook it up and then pull it out.  it is pretty much that simple.  I took mine out the top but I left my heads on and the brackets have eye hooks on them and used them to pull it out.  Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||07-06-2001||11:49 PM||||I removed and re-installed another 2.8L from the top... sooo easy, do like shaun said...  <BR>No you don't have to remove any pully's... I'm not sure about the A/C because I cut mine loose with the dremel, then unbolted it and it fell to the ground, before i removed it or re-installed it in the Smooooth GT.. Steve<P>------------------<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG">   <BR>  with a 100-125HP shot of NOS...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Doni Hagan||07-09-2001||12:31 PM||||Hey, <P>How long did it take to pull from the top? I've got a similar jpb to do and the only way I can get the engine out of my donor car is from the top. Can't drop the cradle I cant jack the car more than a foot or so. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan87GT||07-09-2001||01:41 PM||||Just pulled my V6 and 4speed from the top over the 4th of July. Had to disconnect the alternator and A/C brackets, didn't touch the pully's or water pump. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||07-09-2001||04:15 PM||||Did you leave the exhaust manifolds on when you pulled it out the top?  What about the crossover Y-pipe?||||reg||1
